1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Switching timeframes in TestingView vs TradingView Replay mode:

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,959
On the left: Replay mode.
On the right: TestingView.

3
00:00:08,959 --> 00:00:12,279
They're both on the same date, and both on the 1 minute timeframe

4
00:00:12,279 --> 00:00:16,039
so both charts show the same price: 111.

5
00:00:16,059 --> 00:00:18,939
When we change to a higher timeframe in Replay mode

6
00:00:18,059 --> 00:00:26,139
The full candle is already visible, including its closing price: 112.

7
00:00:27,739 --> 00:00:30,839
When we do the same in TestingView, the system will step back a little

8
00:00:30,839 --> 00:00:36,919
in order to construct the current candle, and will stop at the right time & price, without spoiling it.

9
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:42,640
In replay mode, it's the same for any other timeframe.
Let's take for example the 4h timeframe:

10
00:00:43,099 --> 00:00:47,500
Now you can already see the 4h close: 113,
which is in the future.

11
00:00:50,119 --> 00:00:55,000
In TestingView, switching to 4h timeframe will construct the current 4h candle from its opening time to the current time

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,500
without spoiling the future price action, leaving us at the same price we expect: 111

13
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:06,000
And of course, switching back to our 1 minute chart will show us on the same candle we left off.

14
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:10,500
All this is possible by enabling
one option in TestingView.

15
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:17,959
Go to TestingView options: Prevent candle previews when changing timeframes.
